<!--
    decbench campaign case O2-noinline-libacl-libacl.so.1.1-set_acl_fd (NOVEL
    pool: kuna already tied or beat every rival decompiler on this function and
    the emitted body still was not compilable C, so no other decompiler
    surfaced this fix).

    P9 emission, type rendering.  The `realtypes` relabel (DIV-6, default on)
    rewrites a residual TYPE_UNKNOWN base into a real C type by size:
    undefined1/2/4/8 read char / unsigned short / unsigned int / unsigned long.
    Under a pointer modifier it used to short-circuit to `void` for EVERY size,
    so undefined1 *, undefined4 * and undefined8 * all rendered `void *`.

    Only the DECLARATION was relabelled.  opLoad / opPtradd keep building index
    and cast expressions from the ORIGINAL pointee size, so the declaration and
    the expressions disagreed about the stride:

        int4 set_acl_fd(unsigned long a0,uint a1,uint a2,void *a3)
              if ((code *)a3[1])              // byte offset 1 under GCC's
                a0 = (*(code *)a3[1])(a3,a0); // void-arithmetic extension;
                                              // the expression means offset 8

    gcc -std=gnu11 -fsyntax-only on that body reports "dereferencing 'void *'
    pointer" and "invalid use of void expression".  The source confirms stride
    8: struct error_context is three function pointers at +0/+8/+16.

    The same short-circuit dropped the access width from a store, rendering the
    4-byte errno write in acl_calc_mask as `*(void *)__errno_location() = 0x16;`
    and its 4-byte field write as `*(void *)(v3 + 0x20) = 0x10;`.

    P5 never mis-typed anything: with `option realtypes off` the same parameter
    declares the stride-consistent `xunknown8 *a3` alongside the same `a3[1]`,
    and the stores keep their `xunknown4` width.  The defect was purely the P9
    presentation policy, so the fix makes `void` the FALLBACK under a pointer
    (residual sizes 0/3/5/6/7... with no natural C type) and otherwise relabels
    the pointee through the same size table a scalar uses.

    Stage model: P9 emission, type rendering sub-stage (printc.rs
    realtype_unknown_base, reached from declarator_parts for both the
    declaration front and the cast text).

    No option: this is a correctness fix inside an existing default-on option
    (a declaration that contradicts its own expressions is never desired),
    DIV-47.

    Bytes are libacl.so.1.1.2301 set_acl_fd (0x56c0) and acl_calc_mask
    (0x2820), their PLT/internal callees stubbed as endbr64/ret at their real
    addresses, plus the two .rodata strings set_acl_fd references.

    Pass 1 (default) asserts the fix; pass 2 (`option realtypes off`) pins the
    untouched off path, which shows the same stride with the `xunknownN`
    spelling.  Assertion counts span both passes.
-->
